Why It Happened & Why the Fix Worked:
The system was slow due to excessive background processes, startup applications, and services consuming CPU, memory, and disk resources. Disabling unnecessary
startup programs and services reduced the load on system resources, allowing the operating system to allocate resources more efficiently to active applications.
Reviewing disk usage and system performance settings further optimized system performance, resulting in faster response times and improved overall system stability.

